  {
   "id": "nutrient-absorption",
   "name": {
    "en": "Digestion and absorption in the small intestine",
    "zh-Hant": "小腸的消化與吸收"
   },
   "summary": {
    "en": "Carbohydrate, protein and fat are digested in the lumen and at the brush border, taken up by enterocytes, and leave through the basolateral side. Sugars and amino acids enter the blood capillary and go to the liver. Fat leaves as chylomicrons into the lacteal.",
    "zh-Hant": "碳水化合物、蛋白質與脂肪在腸腔及刷狀緣被消化，由腸細胞吸收，再從基底外側離開。糖與胺基酸進入血液微血管並運往肝臟，脂肪則以乳糜微粒形式進入乳糜管。"
   },
   "cite": ["drozdowski-2006", "miner-williams-2014", "iqbal-2009"],
